    {
      "id": 219475,
      "name": "pwatson1974",
      "username": "pwatson1974",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pwatson1974/{size}/1925_2.png",
      "created_at": "2018-07-18T10:55:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>RtA,</p><p>They’ll announce it when they’re ready to. The information they gave was “not before people are getting OblivAeon”. That gives a floor, likely the next couple of days but no ceiling. At the very least, I would expect them to wait until American’s started getting them, just because Handelabra are a US based company. Waiting until a decent number of people have got it is also reasonable. As, at this stage, is waiting until GenCon when people will have got it, and is the biggest gaming event of the year.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>tl;dr. There’s been no promise it will be now, it will be ‘soon’ so be patient.</p>",
      "post_number": 14,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T05:51:47.656Z",
